 validação de erros","Exemplos de mensagens de erro claras e eficazes","Dicas para criar mensagens de erro personalizadas","Compatibilidade com React, Python e Node.js","Integração com ferramentas de validação de erros","Melhoria da experiência do usuário com mensagens de erro claras"],"ru":["Стиль Гид по сообщениям об ошибках для проверки ошибок","Примеры ясных и эффективных сообщений об ошибках","Советы по созданию персонализированных сообщений об ошибках","Совместимость с React, Python и Node.js","Интеграция с инструментами проверки ошибок","Улучшение пользовательского опыта с ясными сообщениями об ошибках"],"ar":["دليل الأسلوب لرسائل الخطأ للتحقق من الأخطاء","أمثلة لرسائل الخطأ الواضحة والفعالة","نصائح لإنشاء رسائل خطأ مخصصة","التوافق مع React و Python و Node.js","التكامل مع أدوات التحقق من الأخطاء","تحسين تجربة المستخدم مع رسائل الخطأ الواضحة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["AI工具错误消息","错误消息样式指南","验证错误处理","用户体验优化","代码质量提高","AI工具开发","错误处理最佳实践"],"ja":["AIエージェントのエラーメッセージ","エラーメッセージスタイルガイド","バリデーションエラー処理","ユーザーエクスペリエンスの最適化","コード品質の向上","AIエージェントの開発","エラーハンドリングのベストプラクティス"],"ko":["AI 에이전트 오류 메시지","오류 메시지 스타일 가이드","유효성 검사 오류 처리","사용자 경험 최적화","코드 품질 향상","AI 에이전트 개발","오류 처리의 베스트 프랙티스"],"es":["herramientas de AI","guía de estilos para mensajes de error","mejora de la experiencia del usuario","creación de mensajes de error","desarrollo web","alternativas a herramientas de AI","instalación de herramientas de AI","configuración de herramientas de AI"],"fr":["outils d''IA","guide de style pour les messages d''erreur","amélioration de l''expérience utilisateur","création de messages d''erreur","développement web","alternatives aux outils d''IA","installation des outils d''IA","configuration des outils d''IA"],"de":["KI-Tools","Stilguide für Fehlermeldungen","Verbesserung der Benutzererfahrung","Erstellung von Fehlermeldungen","Webentwicklung","Alternativen zu KI-Tools","Installation von KI-Tools","Konfiguration von KI-Tools"],"pt":["ferramentas de IA","mensagens de erro","validação de erros","guia de estilo de mensagens de erro","React","Python","Node.js","como criar mensagens de erro claras","melhor prática para mensagens de erro"],"ru":["ИИ Агенты","сообщения об ошибках","проверка ошибок","Стиль Гид по сообщениям об ошибках","React","Python","Node.js","как создать ясные сообщения об ошибках","лучшая практика для сообщений об ошибках"],"ar":["العمليات التلقائية","رسائل الخطأ","التحقق من الأخطاء","دليل الأسلوب لرسائل الخطأ","React","Python","Node.js","كيفية إنشاء رسائل خطأ واضحة","أفضل ممارسة لرسائل الخطأ"]}},"owner":"github","repo":"gh-aw","repoPath":"github/gh-aw","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-20T04:13:19.578Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"error-messages","description":"Error Message Style Guide for Validation Errors","bodyPreview":"# Error Message Style Guide\n\nThis guide establishes the standard format for validation error messages in the gh-aw codebase. All validation errors should be clear, actionable, and include examples.\n\n## Error Message Template\n\n```\n[what''s wrong]. [what''s expected]. [example of correct usage]\n```\n\nEach error message should answer three questions:\n1. **What''s wrong?** - Clearly state the validation error\n2. **What''s expected?** - Explain the valid format or values\n3. **How to fix it?** - Provide a","body":"# Error Message Style Guide\n\nThis guide establishes the standard format for validation error messages in the gh-aw codebase. All validation errors should be clear, actionable, and include examples.\n\n## Error Message Template\n\n```\n[what''s wrong]. [what''s expected]. [example of correct usage]\n```\n\nEach error message should answer three questions:\n1. **What''s wrong?** - Clearly state the validation error\n2. **What''s expected?** - Explain the valid format or values\n3. **How to fix it?** - Provide a concrete example of correct usage\n\n## Good Examples\n\nThese examples follow the template and provide actionable guidance:\n\n### Time Delta Validation (from time_delta.go)\n```go\nreturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"invalid time delta format: +%s. Expected format like +25h, +3d, +1w, +1mo, +1d12h30m\", deltaStr)\n```\n✅ **Why it''s good:**\n- Clearly identifies the invalid input\n- Lists multiple valid format examples\n- Shows combined formats (+1d12h30m)\n\n### Type Validation with Example\n```go\nreturn \"\", fmt.Errorf(\"manual-approval value must be a string, got %T. Example: manual-approval: \\\"production\\\"\", val)\n```\n✅ **Why it''s good:**\n- Shows actual type received (%T)\n- Provides concrete YAML example\n- Uses proper YAML syntax with quotes\n\n### Enum Validation with Options\n```go\nreturn fmt.Errorf(\"invalid engine: %s. Valid engines are: copilot, claude, codex, custom. Example: engine: copilot\", engineID)\n```\n✅ **Why it''s good:**\n- Lists all valid options\n- Provides simplest example\n- Uses consistent formatting\n\n### MCP Configuration\n```go\nreturn fmt.Errorf(\"tool ''%s'' mcp configuration must specify either ''command'' or ''container''. Example:\\ntools:\\n  %s:\\n    command: \\\"npx @my/tool\\\"\", toolName, toolName)\n```\n✅ **Why it''s good:**\n- Explains mutual exclusivity\n- Shows realistic tool name\n- Formats multi-line YAML example\n\n## Bad Examples\n\nThese examples lack clarity or actionable guidance:\n\n### Too Vague\n```go\nreturn fmt.Errorf(\"invalid format\")\n```\n❌ **Problems:**\n- Doesn''t specify what format is invalid\n- Doesn''t explain expected format\n- No example provided\n\n### Missing Example\n```go\nreturn fmt.Errorf(\"manual-approval value must be a string\")\n```\n❌ **Problems:**\n- States requirement but no example\n- User doesn''t know proper YAML syntax\n- Could be clearer about type received\n\n### Incomplete Information\n```go\nreturn fmt.Errorf(\"invalid engine: %s\", engineID)\n```\n❌ **Problems:**\n- Doesn''t list valid options\n- No guidance on fixing the error\n- User must search documentation\n\n## When to Include Examples\n\nAlways include examples for:\n\n1. **Format/Syntax Errors** - Show the correct syntax\n   ```go\n   fmt.Errorf(\"invalid date format. Expected: YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS. Example: 2024-01-15 14:30:00\")\n   ```\n\n2. **Enum/Choice Fields** - List all valid options\n   ```go\n   fmt.Errorf(\"invalid permission level: %s. Valid levels: read, write, none. Example: permissions:\\n  contents: read\", level)\n   ```\n\n3. **Type Mismatches** - Show expected type and example\n   ```go\n   fmt.Errorf(\"timeout-minutes must be an integer, got %T. Example: timeout-minutes: 10\", value)\n   ```\n\n4. **Complex Configurations** - Provide complete valid example\n   ```go\n   fmt.Errorf(\"invalid MCP server config. Example:\\nmcp-servers:\\n  my-server:\\n    command: \\\"node\\\"\\n    args: [\\\"server.js\\\"]\")\n   ```\n\n## When Examples May Be Optional\n\nExamples can be omitted when:\n\n1. **Error is from wrapped error** - When wrapping another error with context\n   ```go\n   return fmt.Errorf(\"failed to parse configuration: %w\", err)\n   ```\n\n2. **Error is self-explanatory with clear context**\n   ```go\n   return fmt.Errorf(\"duplicate unit ''%s'' in time delta: +%s\", unit, deltaStr)\n   ```\n\n3. **Error points to specific documentation**\n   ```go\n   return fmt.Errorf(\"unsupported feature. See https://docs.example.com/features\")\n   ```\n\n## Formatting Guidelines\n\n### Use Type Verbs for Dynamic Content\n- `%s` - strings\n- `%d` - integers  \n- `%T` - type of value\n- `%v` - general value\n- `%w` - wrapped errors\n\n### Multi-line Examples\nFor YAML configuration examples spanning multiple lines:\n```go\nfmt.Errorf(\"invalid config. Example:\\ntools:\\n  github:\\n    mode: \\\"remote\\\"\")\n```\n\n### Quoting in Examples\nUse proper YAML syntax in examples:\n```go\n// Good - shows quotes when needed\nfmt.Errorf(\"Example: name: \\\"my-workflow\\\"\")\n\n// Good - shows no quotes for simple values\nfmt.Errorf(\"Example: timeout-minutes: 10\")\n```\n\n### Consistent Terminology\nUse the same field names as in YAML:\n```go\n// Good - matches YAML field name\nfmt.Errorf(\"timeout-minutes must be positive\")\n\n// Bad - uses different name\nfmt.Errorf(\"timeout must be positive\")\n```\n\n## Error Message Testing\n\nAll improved error messages should have corresponding tests:\n\n```go\nfunc TestErrorMessageQuality(t *testing.T) {\n    err := validateSomething(invalidInput)\n    require.Error(t, err)\n    \n    // Error should explain what''s wrong\n    assert.Contains(t, err.Error(), \"invalid\")\n    \n    // Error should include expected format or values\n    assert.Contains(t, err.Error(), \"Expected\")\n    \n    // Error should include example\n    assert.Contains(t, err.Error(), \"Example:\")\n}\n```\n\n## Migration Strategy\n\nWhen improving existing error messages:\n\n1. **Identify the error** - Find validation error that lacks clarity\n2. **Analyze context** - Understand what''s being validated\n3. **Apply template** - Add what''s wrong + expected + example\n4. **Add tests** - Verify error message content\n5. **Update comments** - Document the validation logic\n\n## Examples by Category\n\n### Format Validation\n```go\n// Time deltas\nfmt.Errorf(\"invalid time delta format: +%s. Expected format like +25h, +3d, +1w, +1mo, +1d12h30m\", input)\n\n// Dates\nfmt.Errorf(\"invalid date format: %s. Expected: YYYY-MM-DD or relative like -1w. Example: 2024-01-15 or -7d\", input)\n\n// URLs\nfmt.Errorf(\"invalid URL format: %s. Expected: https:// URL. Example: https://api.example.com\", input)\n```\n\n### Type Validation\n```go\n// Boolean expected\nfmt.Errorf(\"read-only must be a boolean, got %T. Example: read-only: true\", value)\n\n// String expected\nfmt.Errorf(\"workflow name must be a string, got %T. Example: name: \\\"my-workflow\\\"\", value)\n\n// Object expected\nfmt.Errorf(\"permissions must be an object, got %T. Example: permissions:\\n  contents: read\", value)\n```\n\n### Choice/Enum Validation\n```go\n// Engine selection\nfmt.Errorf(\"invalid engine: %s. Valid engines: copilot, claude, codex, custom. Example: engine: copilot\", id)\n\n// Permission levels\nfmt.Errorf(\"invalid permission level: %s. Valid levels: read, write, none. Example: contents: read\", level)\n\n// Tool modes\nfmt.Errorf(\"invalid mode: %s. Valid modes: local, remote. Example: mode: \\\"remote\\\"\", mode)\n```\n\n### Configuration Validation\n```go\n// Missing required field\nfmt.Errorf(\"tool ''%s'' missing required ''command'' field. Example:\\ntools:\\n  %s:\\n    command: \\\"node server.js\\\"\", name, name)\n\n// Mutually exclusive fields\nfmt.Errorf(\"cannot specify both ''command'' and ''container''. Choose one. Example: command: \\\"node server.js\\\"\")\n\n// Invalid combination\nfmt.Errorf(\"http MCP servers cannot use ''container'' field. Example:\\ntools:\\n  my-http:\\n    type: http\\n    url: \\\"https://api.example.com\\\"\")\n```\n\n## References\n\n- **Excellent example to follow**: `pkg/workflow/time_delta.go`\n- **Pattern inspiration**: Go standard library error messages\n- **Testing examples**: `pkg/workflow/*_test.go`\n\n## Tools\n\nWhen writing error messages, consider:\n- The user''s perspective (what do they need to fix it?)\n- The context (where in the workflow is the error?)\n- The documentation (should we reference specific docs?)\n- The complexity (is multi-line example needed?)\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-02T09:50:28.302Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for AI Agents like Cursor and AutoGPT needing standardized validation error message generation for clear user feedback.","zh":"适合像Cursor和AutoGPT这样的AI代理，需要标准化的验证错误消息生成以提供清晰的用户反馈。","ja":"CursorやAutoGPTのようなAIエージェントに適しており、ユーザーに明確なフィードバックを提供するために標準化されたバリデーションエラーメッセージを生成する必要があります。","ko":"Cursor와 AutoGPT 같은 AI 에이전트에 적합하며, 명확한 사용자 피드백을 제공하기 위해 표준화된 검증 오류 메시지 생성이 필요합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de IA como Cursor y AutoGPT que necesitan generación de mensajes de error de validación estandarizados para una retroalimentación clara del usuario.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents IA comme Cursor et AutoGPT nécessitant une génération de messages d''erreur de validation standardisés pour une rétroaction claire de l''utilisateur.","de":"Ideal für KI-Agents wie Cursor und AutoGPT, die eine standardisierte Generierung von Validierungsfehlernachrichten für eine klare Benutzerfeedback benötigen.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de IA como Cursor e AutoGPT que necessitam de geração de mensagens de erro de validação padronizadas para feedback de usuário claro.","ru":"Идеально для агентов ИИ, таких как Cursor и AutoGPT, требующих стандартизированного генерирования сообщений об ошибках проверки для четкой обратной связи пользователя.","ar":"مثالي لعميل الأجنتات الذكية مثل Cursor و AutoGPT التي تحتاج إلى إنتاج رسائل خطأ التحقق المعيارية لتعزيز تجربة المستخدم"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to create clear, actionable error messages using a standardized template, including what''s wrong, what''s expected, and examples of correct usage, utilizing GitHub Agentic Workflows and validation error protocols.","zh":"赋予代理创建清晰、可操作的错误消息的能力，使用标准化模板，包括出错原因、预期结果和正确使用示例，利用GitHub Agentic Workflows和验证错误协议。","ja":"GitHub Agentic Workflowsとバリデーションエラープロトコルを利用し、標準化されたテンプレートを使用して、エラーの原因、期待される結果、正しい使用方法の例など、明確で操作可能なエラーメッセージを作成できるようにエージェントをEmpowerします。","ko":"GitHub Agentic Workflows와 검증 오류 프로토콜을 활용하여 표준화된 템플릿을 사용하여 에러의 원인, 예상 결과 및 올바른 사용 예제 등을 포함한 명확하고 실행 가능한 오류 메시지를 생성할 수 있는 에이전트의 능력을 강화합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a crear mensajes de error claros y accionables utilizando una plantilla estandarizada, incluyendo qué está mal, qué se espera y ejemplos de uso correcto, utilizando GitHub Agentic Workflows y protocolos de error de validación.","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer des messages d''erreur clairs et actionnables en utilisant un modèle standardisé, y compris ce qui ne va pas, ce qui est attendu et des exemples d''utilisation correcte, en utilisant GitHub Agentic Workflows et les protocoles d''erreur de validation.","de":"Ermöglicht es den Agents, klare und handhabbare Fehlermeldungen mit einer standardisierten Vorlage zu erstellen, einschließlich dessen, was falsch ist, was erwartet wird und Beispiele für die korrekte Verwendung, unter Verwendung von GitHub Agentic Workflows und Validierungsfehlerprotokollen.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a criarem mensagens de erro claras e ações utilizando um modelo padronizado, incluindo o que está errado, o que é esperado e exemplos de uso correto, utilizando GitHub Agentic Workflows e protocolos de erro de validação.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью создавать четкие и действенные сообщения об ошибках, используя стандартизированный шаблон, включая то, что не так, что ожидается и примеры правильного использования, используя GitHub Agentic Workflows и протоколы ошибок проверки.","ar":"تمكين الوكلاء من إنشاء رسائل خطأ واضحة وقابلة للتنفيذ باستخدام قالب معياري، بما في ذلك ما هو الخطأ، وما هو المتوقع، وأمثلة للاستخدام الصحيح، باستخدام GitHub Agentic Workflows وبروتوكولات خطأ التحقق"},"useCases":{"en":["Generating informative validation errors","Standardizing error message formats across applications","Improving user experience through clear error feedback"],"zh":["生成信息丰富的验证错误","标准化应用程序中的错误消息格式","通过清晰的错误反馈提高用户体验"],"ja":["情報の豊富なバリデーションエラーを生成する","アプリケーション全体でエラーメッセージのフォーマットを標準化する","明確なエラーフィードバックを通じてユーザーエクスペリエンスを向上させる"],"ko":["정보가 풍부한 검증 오류를 생성하는こと","애플리케이션 전반에서 오류 메시지 형식을 표준화하는 것","명확한 오류 피드백을 통해 사용자 경험을 향상시키는 것"],"es":["Generación de errores de validación informativos","Establecimiento de formatos de mensajes de error estandarizados en aplicaciones","Mejora de la experiencia del usuario a través de una retroalimentación de error clara"],"fr":["Génération de messages d''erreur de validation informatifs","Standardisation des formats de messages d''erreur dans les applications","Amélioration de l''expérience utilisateur grâce à une rétroaction d''erreur claire"],"de":["Generierung von informativen Validierungsfehlern","Standardisierung von Fehlermeldungsformaten in Anwendungen","Verbesserung der Benutzererfahrung durch klare Fehlerfeedback"],"pt":["Geração de erros de validação informativos","Padronização de formatos de mensagens de erro em aplicativos","Melhoria da experiência do usuário por meio de feedback de erro claro"],"ru":["Генерирование информативных сообщений об ошибках проверки","Стандартизация форматов сообщений об ошибках в приложениях","Улучшение пользовательского опыта за счет четкой обратной связи об ошибках"],"ar":["إنتاج رسائل خطأ التحقق الإعلامية","تحديد معايير أنماط رسائل الخطأ عبر التطبيقات","تحسين تجربة المستخدم من خلال إرجاع الملاحظات حول الأخطاء بوضوح"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires implementation of the error message template","Limited to validation error messages","Dependent on gh-aw codebase integration"],"zh":["需要实现错误消息模板","仅限于验证错误消息","依赖于gh-aw代码库集成"],"ja":["エラーメッセージテンプレートの実装が必要","バリデーションエラーメッセージのみ","gh-awコードベースの統合に依存"],"ko":["오류 메시지 템플릿의 구현이 필요","검증 오류 메시지만 해당","gh-aw 코드베이스 통합에 의존"],"es":["Requiere la implementación de la plantilla de mensaje de error","Limitado a mensajes de error de validación","Dependiente de la integración de la base de código gh-aw"],"fr":["Nécessite la mise en œuvre du modèle de message d''erreur","Limité aux messages d''erreur de validation","Dépendant de l''intégration du codebase gh-aw"],"de":["Erfordert die Implementierung der Fehlermeldungsvorlage","Begrenzt auf Validierungsfehlermeldungen","Abhängig von der Integration des gh-aw-Codebases"],"pt":["Requer implementação do modelo de mensagem de erro","Limitado a mensagens de erro de validação","Dependente da integração do código gh-aw"],"ru":["Требует реализации шаблона сообщения об ошибке","Ограничен сообщениями об ошибках проверки","Зависит от интеграции кодовой базы gh-aw"],"ar":["يتطلب تنفيذ نموذج رسالة الخطأ","محدود برسائل خطأ التحقق","يعتمد على دمج قاعدة الكود gh-aw"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"335bea0426f18dc9185bf3c0fa9b369c8f752ef68d0048c8c6dd4075d3375978","qualityScore":70}');
